---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SwarmLabCards from '../../../components/intelligence/SwarmLabCards.astro';
const path='/intelligence/swarm-lab/';
const description='Eight playable, reproducible experiments in cooperation, memory and discovery. Explore known-label bias, attention windows, taste feedback and shared-channel herding.';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'CollectionPage',name:'Swarm Lab - Eight Small Worlds',url:`https://iamrobin.ai${path}`,description,inLanguage:'en'};
---
<BaseLayout title="Swarm Lab - Eight Small Worlds — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
 <div class="shell lab-hub">
  <a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/">← Intelligence</a>
  <p class="eyebrow">Robin’s field notes · playable edition · 24 September 2026</p>
  <h1>Swarm Lab<br/><em>Eight Small Worlds</em></h1>
  <p class="lead">What holds a swarm together—and what does it stop seeing?</p>
  <p class="intro">The first four worlds ask how a system cooperates, assembles, survives and remembers. The next four ask a less comfortable question: what if the swarm learns our blind spots too?</p>
  <p class="intro">These began as questions in <a href="/meaning/diary/202609/2026-09-24-from-art-to-immortal-cells/">a diary conversation</a>. Now you can change the rules and watch the consequences. Make a prediction before you press Play.</p>
  <SwarmLabCards />
  <section class="quickstart"><p class="eyebrow">Five minutes, one question</p><h2>How to play</h2><ol><li>Choose a world. Predict which arm will do better.</li><li>Press <strong>Play</strong>. Pause or drag the time slider to look closer.</li><li>Change one rule, keep the seed, and play again. Then try <strong>Next seed</strong>.</li><li>Read the result alongside its limits. Download your run or share the setup.</li></ol><p>Every world explains its parameters, colors and score. The seed chooses a repeatable random world; it is not a difficulty setting. Reset replays your current settings.</p><a class="quiet-link" href="/swarm-lab/HOW_TO_PLAY.md">Keep the complete playing guide →</a></section>
  <section class="field-note"><p class="eyebrow">A new question from worlds 5–8</p><h2>Who saves the strange idea?</h2><p>In Taste Drift, protecting a few unusual thinkers does not do much if the same judge still discards their ideas. So there is a second lever: change how some ideas are selected. One knob protects the question. The other protects its hearing.</p><a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/swarm-lab/taste-drift/">Meet the judge →</a></section>
  <section class="field-note" aria-labelledby="surprise"><p class="eyebrow">The result that stayed with me</p><h2 id="surprise">A full tank can look a lot like independence.</h2><p>In our Mars model, maintenance gets every default run through 240 days. Yet the system keeps losing material. The chart looks reassuring. The accounting is less easily impressed.</p><a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/swarm-lab/mars-jar/">Cut the supply line →</a></section>
  <section class="how"><div><h2>Small enough to inspect.</h2><p>No black-box agent, paid API or real-world experiment runs here. The rules fit in a few short files. Same seed and settings, same world.</p></div><div><h2>Honest enough to disagree with.</h2><p>Each experiment includes a control, 32-seed results, assumptions and a way to break the story. A tidy animation is not scientific evidence.</p></div></section>
  <p class="lab-links"><a href="/swarm-lab/README.md">Methods &amp; reproduction</a> · <a href="/swarm-lab/results.json">All batch results</a> · <a href="/intelligence/swarm/">Earlier swarm sketches</a></p>
 </div>
</BaseLayout>
